// REJECTS: Field 'mappings' is required
//
// `mappings:` is required on a Runtime and on a SingleConnectionRuntime; `connections:` and
// `connectionStores:` are both optional. The grammar requires none of them -- the body is
// `(mappings | connections | connectionStoresList)*` -- so this too is a walker rule.
//
// The asymmetry is the point: a runtime with connections and no mappings looks more useful
// than one with mappings and no connections, and it is the illegal one. A rewrite that
// treats all three as optional accepts it.
###Runtime
Runtime fixture::neg::NoMappings
{
   connections:
   [
      fixture::neg::Db:
      [
         c1: fixture::neg::Conn
      ]
   ];
}
